      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Fungal Forest [zone=712]\n**Who:**\n- Adeenas [ _Quest, Mission_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Lisaryn's Remains [item=86865]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Autoros [npc=34826]\n- Deagus the Fungrotect [ _Quests_]\n- Eulyris [npc=34829]\n- Excrug Shrivstem [ _Quests_]\n**Era:** | !Underfoot\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Jan 5 19:11:33 2010\nModified: Tue Nov 11 09:32:35 2025 | | This solo task begins with Adeena [npc=34813] in the Fungal Forest. She is a telmira located at -905, -850, 95 (southeastern area of the zone). Keep a lookout while speaking with her as KoS mobs wander the area.\nYou say, 'Hail, Adeenas'\nAdeenas says 'Hello! I am Adeenas of the telmira. I see you must be lost. Perhaps you should get your bearings here before you further travel the Fungal Forest. Like most of the Underfoot, this place is dangerous to outsiders. This is more true if you venture further to the east, or if you choose to trifle with the sporali or cliknar. Perhaps you came by to [chat] with me instead?'\nYou say, 'Let's have a chat'\nAdeenas says 'I love talking to new people! I get so lonely these days, since the sporali became violent and the cliknar invaded the forest. The other telmira have scattered to the winds, it seems, and I don't know what to do next. No matter. I have you to talk to now. You can remain here and talk with me [forever], yes?'\nYou say, 'Forever...'\nAdeenas says 'Yes! You can remain here forever--if you'll let me transform you into a telmira like me with my special spell, of course; and whatever fate comes to the telmira, you will share. Does that sound [fun]? We can fly to the tops of mushrooms, skim the gullies of rivers, sing songs honoring the life of the forest, and eat fruit beneath the weeping spore caps.'\nYou say, 'No, that doesn't sound like fun...'\nAdeenas says 'You mortals are all the same. What sounds like fun to a telmira only seems to scare you to death, yet you all seem to embrace the most terrifying and random type of existence. Well, you don't know what you're missing, that's all I can say! Since you're going to stick with your mortal experience of death and danger, how about helping me with a [favor]? Or did you already do that for me? If so, perhaps it's time to do something about [Rakkirin].'\nYou say, 'A favor?'\nAdeenas says 'As I mentioned before, the other telmira kin have gotten separated by the recent disturbances in the forest. Brell's thoughts have gone away somewhere and not returned. While we long for his presence to come back and set these matters right, I fear I cannot wait any longer. I must know what has become of my kin before something else unforeseen and terrible happens. I cannot go looking for them myself, with the [sporali] having gone mad. Would you be so [kind] as to find them all for me, or at least what happened to them?'\nYou say, 'I would be so kind'\nAdeenas says 'Oh, thank you! You are so kind. I will certainly write an epic poem in your honor once you finish my dangerous and life-threatening errand!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Fate of the Telmira'.\nAdeenas hasn't heard from any fellow telmira kin since Rakkiren Shrivstem took control of the sporali. Help Adeenas locate the missing telmira, or if that is not possible, at least find out what happened to them.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Explore the northwestern corner of the Forest for signs of Autoros 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nThis step updates at /way +1425,+2315,+430 where Autoros [npc=34826] is.\n2\\. Hail Autoros 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Autoros'\nAutoros says 'Adeenas sent you? I am Autoros of the telmira. Though I was nearly killed by the invading cliknar and by the warring sporali factions, I have been fortunate enough to remain hidden in this refuge, at least for now. Tell Adeenas not to worry about me. We must, however, make every effort to call out to Brell Serilis, for his absence is allowing havoc to be unleashed upon the Fungal Forest. If things continue to spin out of control, the fertility of this place will cease, and entire worlds will start to die.'\n3\\. Explore the southwestern corner of the Forest for signs of Eulyris 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nThis step updates at /way -410,+2020,+430 where Eulyris [npc=34829] is.\n4\\. Hail Eulyris 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Eulyris'\nEulyris says 'You may call me Eulyris. I have sequestered myself in this area in the hopes that the mad sporali will avoid me. Barbarous things they do in the name self-enlightenment. The balance has been upset drastically and grows worse all the time. Please let Adeenas know that I am all right, and when the time comes I will be ready to join our power to call Brell Serilis, if indeed he still exists.'\n5\\. Explore the southern-central corner of the Forest for signs of Vaelani 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nThis step updates at /way -790,+1165,+230 where Excrug Shrivstem [npc=34820] is.\n6\\. Hail Excrug Shrivstem 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nYour task 'Fate of the Telmira' has been updated.\nExcrug Shrivstem says 'I am Excrug. I found Vaelani fleeing from us and aided with the capture. Vaelani has been reduced to a primal essence and is now in the possession of my master, Rakkirin. I trust Vaelani can be restored to normal without harm. I admit that some of Rakkirin's orders cause me anguish and suffering. I do not wish to harm the creatures of the Forest or do things that Brell Serilis might find upsetting.'\n7\\. Explore the northern-central edge of the Forest for signs of Lisaryn 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nThis step updates at /way -778,+1108,+213 near where Deagus the Fungrotect [npc=34844] is.\n8\\. Hail Deagus the Fungrotect 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Deagus the Fungrotect'\nDeagus the Fungrotect says 'Bah, found Deagus you have. These creatures are destroying themselves. It's no worse than anything else happening in the Underfoot, but certainly no better. I came this way a few days ago, aware that the cliknar appeared to be burrowing into the Forest; but then the sporali seemed to go crazy, and they started killing each other and chasing the telmira around. I saw several of them kill one of the telmira here. It was the saddest and most despicable thing I ever saw. I was too late to come to its aid. Here are the remains, in case one of the other telmira should be interested.'\nYou receive Lisaryn's Remains [item=86865].\n9\\. Deliver Lisaryn's Remains to Adeena 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nYour task 'Fate of the Telmira' has been updated.\nAdeenas says 'Oh, no! Lisaryn is dead! It will take years for Lisaryn's spirit to regather essence and be reborn! Oh, if only Brell Serilis were here, awful things like this would never happen!'\n10\\. Hail Adeenas 0/1 (Fungal Forest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Adeenas'\nYou have helped Adeenas determine where the other telmira have gone, or what might have happened to them. This may help Adeenas come up with an idea for dealing with the sporali and cliknar menaces later.\nAdeenas says 'You have helped me immensely! I must think about what has happened, and perhaps with the help of the remaining telmira sages I can figure out how to rescue poor Vaelani from Rakkirin's clutches. Now, for you, I shall uphold my promise and get started on my epic poem that will glorify your name!'\n_Rewards:_\n210 platinum\nExperience\n40 Brellium Tokens [item=88944]\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]",
